{% import 'landing/sections/_shot.html.twig' as shot %}

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════ YOUR ROLE ═══════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="role-section" id="your-role">
    <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-label">Your Role</div>
        <h2 class="section-title">You're the owner. Not the gaffer.</h2>
        <p class="section-sub">Step into the boardroom and build a football powerhouse from the ground up — you don't just manage the pitch, you run the entire institution. Start at the very bottom of an {{ world.totals.tierCount }}-tier national ladder in a club of your choosing, create your owner — name, nationality, the lot — and take charge of a modest setup: a basic squad, a handful of introductory coaches, and foundational backroom staff. Direct the club's revenue across recruitment, staff, and world-class infrastructure, and play the long game.</p>

        <div class="point-list" style="margin-top:32px;">
            <div class="point">
                <span class="point-title">Your Personal Assistant</span>
                <p>Not a hire — your own briefing. One glance gives you dressing room harmony, squad fitness and tactical readiness, supporter sentiment, and active scouting status, all pulled live from the same data your staff work from.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="point">
                <span class="point-title is-mint">Dressing Room Harmony</span>
                <p>Real-time pulse of team chemistry and player morale — see it on the squad's relationship network before it becomes a dressing-room problem.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="point">
                <span class="point-title is-plain">Tactical &amp; Physical Health</span>
                <p>Squad fitness and tactical readiness at a glance, so you know if the XI your Manager wants is actually fit to put out.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="point">
                <span class="point-title is-red">Supporter Pulse</span>
                <p>Fan sentiment, attendance and community outlook — the crowd notices every decision you make as much as the board does.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="role-grid" style="margin-top:32px;">
            <div class="role-col role-col-owner">
                <div class="role-col-title">YOU CONTROL</div>
                <ul class="role-list">
                    <li>Capital allocation &amp; financial decisions</li>
                    <li>Facility investment &amp; infrastructure build-out</li>
                    <li>Staff hiring across 6 distinct roles</li>
                    <li>Sponsor negotiations &amp; investor equity deals</li>
                    <li>Agent &amp; guardian relations</li>
                    <li>Club identity, kit colours &amp; strategic direction</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="role-col role-col-staff">
                <div class="role-col-title">YOUR STAFF HANDLE</div>
                <ul class="role-list">
                    <li><span class="role-staff-name">Chairman</span>Agrees the season mandate with your Manager — his job security hinges on hitting it. Signs off Facility Manager discounts and investor offers, balances the operating reserve, and plans excursions to keep the squad onside.</li>
                    <li><span class="role-staff-name">Director of Football</span>Recruitment priorities, scouting reach, and the free-agent panic button when a position can't field an XI. Manages coach and scout contracts, including individual coach-to-player assignments.</li>
                    <li><span class="role-staff-name">Manager</span>Formation, playing style &amp; matchday selection. Resolves squad conflicts and player requests — override him anytime, at a morale cost.</li>
                    <li><span class="role-staff-name">Facility Manager</span>Proactive or reactive maintenance — stop campus decay before it hits performance and player morale.</li>
                    <li><span class="role-staff-name">Scout</span>Talent identification, evaluation ability &amp; player reports.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        {# Paired with the closing text rather than dropped underneath it on its
           own — a lone tall phone shot centred under a full-width block reads as
           an orphan and leaves a column of dead space either side. #}
        <div class="feature-split is-reversed" style="margin-top:32px;">
            <figure class="feature-shot">
                {{ shot.img('chairman-duties', 'The Chairman staff screen — duties include agreeing the season mandate, signing off Facility Manager discounts and investor offers, and setting the minimum operating reserve', false, 340, '2026-10') }}
                <figcaption>Your Chairman's duties, and the auto-decide switch if you'd rather not be asked</figcaption>
            </figure>

            <p class="role-footer" style="margin-top:0;">Delegate everything to your DoF and Manager and focus on the boardroom — or override every decision yourself. The level of involvement is always your choice. Promotion means your decisions worked, not just your tactics. One warning: staff whose morale collapses will resign, and a backroom departure damages squad-wide morale and erases relationships that took seasons to build.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
